WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Gemini 4 Carbon Scores 59, a head of clawed in gpt6 for cyber teams first. This is MAG 7 Daily, episode 37. After that model, a touch screen mac, a fresh Alexa set, then a September cloud thread. Google ship Gemini 4 Carbon on top of argon, out only two weeks, and Korei Kavook Chulglue at deep mine called it the lab's strongest model for cyber work and jobs that run a long time. Selected defense teams get it this week, then fair wind partners, while google

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.780
stays in Washington's voluntary pre-release tests.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.020
Argonne is already in the Gemini app and AI search.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.620
No public date for a wide-carbon release.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.960
Engadget and the follow-ups put the index jump at 9 points from Argonne's 50.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.300
On Google's own cyber tests, vulnerability detection is 88.2%.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.360
Exploit validation 54.8 and patching 71.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.700
Secure code success is more than twice Argonne.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.360
The Chrome team told Google its patches beat another lab's frontier model by more than

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.120
10 times.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:09.340
The opening token price matches Argon, $2 per million in, $10 per million out, and cashed

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.040
input 95% cheaper.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.340
Basic tutorial says those rates later go to $4.20.

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:22.803
Apple's first touchscreen Mac is the MacBook Pro with a Pro LED XDR panel, in 14 and 16

00:01:22.803 --> 00:01:25.943
inch sizes, and it is also the first Mac with OLED.

00:01:25.943 --> 00:01:33.063
Bangkok Post lists 2,000 nits, a 10 million to 1 contrast ratio, a 120 Hertz refresh

00:01:33.063 --> 00:01:39.563
that can fall to 10, P3 and Adobe RGB up to 24 hours of battery, and a chassis between

00:01:39.563 --> 00:01:48.043
1.36 and 1.81 kilograms. The chips are M5 Pro and M5 Max, with up to 128 gigabytes of

00:01:48.043 --> 00:01:55.143
memory and 16 terabytes of storage, plus 50% deeper base, Thunderbolt 5, and a 12 megapixel

00:01:55.143 --> 00:01:59.923
center-stage camera. Touch sits in the panel, and Dynamic Island comes to the Mac.

00:02:00.463 --> 00:02:09.263
NewsCord prices the 14-inch from $2,899, and the 16-inch from $3,399, with a loaded machine

00:02:09.263 --> 00:02:16.843
at $14,549. The information says a current MacBook Pro without touch starts at $1,999,

00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:24.323
and Mac rumors puts a $400 premium on the OLED models versus comparable Mini-LED ones. Pre-orders

00:02:24.323 --> 00:02:29.963
is open October 30th. The launch day is November 6th. Johnny Sruji called it a monumental

00:02:29.963 --> 00:02:35.043
step for the Mac. John Ternis introduced it after taking over from Tim Cook last month.

00:02:35.743 --> 00:02:41.183
NewsCord also dug up the old objections. Steve Jobs said a touchscreen Mac was ergonomically

00:02:41.183 --> 00:02:46.543
terrible and that your arm wants to fall off, and Tim Cook once likened fusing a laptop and

00:02:46.543 --> 00:02:52.307
a tablet to a refrigerator and a toaster. Amazon on Wednesday put five new Alexa devices

00:02:52.307 --> 00:02:56.207
on sale and the same day confirmed job cuts in devices.

00:02:56.867 --> 00:03:05.007
Silicon UK and market screener list an Echo show 16 from $499.99 with Fire TV and a

00:03:05.007 --> 00:03:05.987
night vision camera.

00:03:06.627 --> 00:03:10.727
An Echo studio at $249.99 with a camera.

00:03:11.327 --> 00:03:15.947
An Echo Dot at $99.99 with a hub and a Wi-Fi extender.

00:03:16.447 --> 00:03:22.187
An Echo Time at $199.99 that senses light sleep and wakes you without a

00:03:22.187 --> 00:03:29.427
wearable, and an Alexa photo frame from the same $199.99, pulling pictures from Amazon

00:03:29.427 --> 00:03:34.787
photos. Amazon told Silicon UK that cut was a small number of roles and said it would

00:03:34.787 --> 00:03:40.447
improve efficiency. Reuters citing an unnamed person familiar with the matter, put devices

00:03:40.447 --> 00:03:47.007
and services losses at up to 250 people, mostly software, after about 1,000 retail cuts

00:03:47.007 --> 00:03:54.207
earlier this month. The hardware next door is Apple's $299 home view, and a $149 home

00:03:54.207 --> 00:03:59.967
pod mini-2 on the latest Siri. Market screener also notes OpenAI is building hardware of

00:03:59.967 --> 00:04:06.507
its own. Microsoft is leaving television sets. FlatPanels HD says Copilot is being pulled

00:04:06.507 --> 00:04:12.867
because AI on smart TVs fail to take off, and KuCoin says LG is discontinuing that Copilot

00:04:12.867 --> 00:04:19.267
service on its sets. A few more filings and launches. Bloomberg, via 9 to 5 Mac, says Apple

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:24.547
and Microsoft must now store users' communications in Russia and hand them to security agencies

00:04:24.547 --> 00:04:30.647
have asked. Judge Edward DeVilla set the schedule, including a trial date, in Apple's trade secrets

00:04:30.647 --> 00:04:37.787
case against two former employees, OpenAI and IO products. PCMag says meta-delayed an update amid

00:04:37.787 --> 00:04:40.987
concern about scraping websites for possible AI training.

00:04:41.607 --> 00:04:46.507
Nvidia unveiled DSX pod server racks meant to speed AI factory buildouts.

00:04:47.107 --> 00:04:51.467
Google DeepMind and Google Cloud are deploying AI across Singapore's health system.

00:04:52.454 --> 00:04:56.634
The 59 on that composite index does not hold on the job's buyer's run.

00:04:57.434 --> 00:05:02.694
Biggo Finance says carbon with Google's anti-gravity tools scored 59 on agentic coding,

00:05:03.254 --> 00:05:06.314
behind-clawed code with Opus 5.5 at 62.

00:05:06.314 --> 00:05:16.674
On Frontier SWE2, GPT-6 Astra led at 65.5% against Carbon 61.2. On the Val's mix of

00:05:16.674 --> 00:05:24.074
finance, coding, legal, and tax work, Carbon was second at 70.36%, behind Sonnet 5.5

00:05:24.074 --> 00:05:32.054
at 70.85, and on WebDev Arena it finished fourth. Those three Cyberheadlines, including 54.8%

00:05:32.054 --> 00:05:38.174
on a 10-hour exploit gym test were measured with safety guardrails off. The defensive chain Google

00:05:38.174 --> 00:05:43.764
is selling was not scored in the setup a customer would be allowed to run. Google Cloud revenue

00:05:43.764 --> 00:05:49.404
more than doubled in the September quarter passed $30 billion and operating income there tripled

00:05:49.404 --> 00:05:58.084
to $11.12 billion. Azure in the same period was $33 billion, up 48%. Yesterday the open question

00:05:58.084 --> 00:06:02.644
on this show was still the growth rate. Those two lines answer it, and they leave the

00:06:02.644 --> 00:06:07.844
old number three cloud a few billion dollars from Azure. The information says Alphabet's

00:06:07.844 --> 00:06:14.724
company revenue rose 25% to 127.58 billion dollars, a bit under Wall Street forecasts.

00:06:15.544 --> 00:06:20.444
Free cash flow went negative by more than $9 billion, against more than $24 billion

00:06:20.444 --> 00:06:22.104
dollars positive a year earlier.

00:06:22.744 --> 00:06:26.284
Search ads grew 12% to $63.35 billion.

00:06:26.984 --> 00:06:30.624
The softest stretch for that business since the second quarter of 2025.

00:06:31.664 --> 00:06:36.184
Sundar Pachai said search queries are growing year over year at the fastest pace in five

00:06:36.184 --> 00:06:38.564
years, and he credited AI spending.

00:06:39.304 --> 00:06:44.404
Philip Schindler told analysts the AI mode surge hurt the ad result because monetization there

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:44.884
is lower.

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:49.424
Google is not placing as many ads in AI mode as an ordinary search.

00:06:49.424 --> 00:06:55.364
This is not a pure hosting comparison. Google Cloud's total includes tensor processing units

00:06:55.364 --> 00:07:00.804
that customers install in their own data centers. Thomas Curian said demand is extraordinary.

00:07:01.504 --> 00:07:06.704
Executives told analysts to expect those chip sales to count for even more of Google Cloud next year.

00:07:07.504 --> 00:07:14.644
Microsoft's September revenue rose 19% to $92.3 billion. One percentage point faster than the prior

00:07:14.644 --> 00:07:21.524
quarter, a figure digitimes also carried. Microsoft 365 commercial cloud, co-pilot plus

00:07:21.524 --> 00:07:28.064
the rest of office, rose 17% to 27.7 billion dollars. A slight pickup from June.

00:07:28.744 --> 00:07:34.064
What Microsoft did not repeat was the paid co-pilot seat count. 30 million at the end of June,

00:07:34.364 --> 00:07:40.224
up from 15 million at the end of 2025, each paying $30 a month on top of the app fees.

00:07:40.224 --> 00:07:46.604
Sachi and Adela said customers paying for usage-based co-pilot features grew 75% in the quarter.

00:07:47.344 --> 00:07:50.864
Amy Hood said revenue per user rose on that pay-as-you-go use.

00:07:51.464 --> 00:07:57.164
Late last month, Microsoft folded co-pilot into one app, partly to push agents and usage billing,

00:07:57.644 --> 00:08:01.884
including tools set against Meta's Muse. Same build, two proofs.

00:08:02.344 --> 00:08:05.864
Google's cash flow went negative while cloud operating income tripled,

00:08:06.264 --> 00:08:09.104
and part of that cloud line is now chips leaving the building.

00:08:09.104 --> 00:08:14.084
Microsoft kept commercial cloud growth in the teens and stopped publishing the seat count

00:08:14.084 --> 00:08:17.404
that had been the simple evidence subscriptions were absorbing the spend.

00:08:17.924 --> 00:08:20.464
Curians marker for the next shift is next year.

00:08:21.555 --> 00:08:27.395
On the calendar, newscord says touchscreen MacBook Pro pre-orders open October 30th, and the

00:08:27.395 --> 00:08:29.595
machine's launch November 6th.

